    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d497">

                <pb facs="0539" n="527" sameAs="frus:frus1937v01/pg527"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">352.1121 Fernandez, Antonio/59: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Consul at Gibraltar</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Williams</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-07-17T14:00:00-04:00">July 17, 1937—2 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>For Fisher. Your 9th via Marseille<anchor n="82" xml:id="d497-f1"/> and 17th via
                    Gibraltar. We preferred if possible to effect arrangements for evacuation of
                    interested persons before considering sending a naval vessel to Palma. In view
                    of commanding general’s attitude you should continue efforts to <pb facs="0540"
                        n="528" xml:id="pg528"/> obtain specific list of charges against Fernandez
                    and report developments.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
